# Bundle G — Public / community. NOT ACTIVE.
#
# This is an example. GitHub only reads `.github/FUNDING.yml`, so nothing here
# renders a Sponsor button. To enable:
#
#   git mv .github/bundles/community/FUNDING.yml.example .github/FUNDING.yml
#
# It is in the bundle mostly so the question has an answer. A ScaleMeNow
# repository is commercial work, and a Sponsor button on it asks the public to
# fund a company — which reads as confusion about what the repository is, not as
# an invitation. Leave this off unless the repository is a genuinely
# community-maintained open source project with its own maintainers.
#
# Uncomment only the lines you will actually use. An empty key is rendered as a
# dead link, and a Sponsor button that goes nowhere is worse than no button.
# Full syntax: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/displaying-a-sponsor-button-in-your-repository

# github: [ORG_OR_USERNAME]
# open_collective: COLLECTIVE_SLUG
# custom: ["https://example.com/sponsor"]
